Grep confirms `itemHoverStyle` appears only at lines 227 and 245; `pathEmphasisState` only at 244-245.

## Fix — Option A (recommended, 2 small edits)

Reuse the already-imported helper `setStatesStylesFromModel` (imported at `RadarView.ts:21`, and already used at lines 201/202). Its default `styleType` is `'itemStyle'` and it loops `OTHER_STATES = ['emphasis', 'blur', 'select']` calling `model.getItemStyle()` per state (`src/util/states.ts:797-820`), i.e. exactly `emphasis.itemStyle` / `blur.itemStyle` / `select.itemStyle`.

**Edit 1** — `RadarView.ts:226-227`, delete the now-unused precomputed emphasis style.

old:
```ts
            const emphasisModel = itemModel.getModel('emphasis');
            const itemHoverStyle = emphasisModel.getModel('itemStyle').getItemStyle();
```
new:
```ts
            const emphasisModel = itemModel.getModel('emphasis');
```

(Keep `emphasisModel` — it is still used at line 263 for `focus` / `blurScope` / `disabled`.)

**Edit 2** — `RadarView.ts:244-245`.

old:
```ts
                const pathEmphasisState = symbolPath.ensureState('emphasis');
                pathEmphasisState.style = zrUtil.clone(itemHoverStyle);
```
new:
```ts
                setStatesStylesFromModel(symbolPath, itemModel);
```

No `zrUtil.clone` is needed: `getItemStyle()` returns a freshly built object on every call (`makeStyleMapper` at `src/model/mixin/makeStyleMapper.ts:37-52` allocates `const style = {}` each invocation), so each symbol gets its own state style objects. Line 245 was the only `zrUtil.clone` use in the file, but `zrUtil` remains used (`defaults`, `each`, `extend`, `map`) so the import at line 22 stays.

Types check out with no changes: `itemModel` is `Model<RadarSeriesDataItemOption>` (line 181) and is already passed to `setStatesStylesFromModel` at lines 201-202, so it satisfies `Model<Partial<Record<'emphasis' | 'blur' | 'select', any>>>`. `RadarSymbol` = `(ECSymbol | ZRImage) & { __dimIdx: number }`; both branches of the union extend `Displayable`, satisfying the `el: Displayable` parameter.

## Fix — Option B (explicit, if you prefer to keep the styles hoisted out of the per-symbol loop)

Behaviourally identical; avoids 3 `getItemStyle()` calls per symbol (radar renders `indicatorCount × seriesDataCount` symbols).

Replace `RadarView.ts:226-227` with:
```ts
            const emphasisModel = itemModel.getModel('emphasis');
            const emphasisItemStyle = emphasisModel.getModel('itemStyle').getItemStyle();
            const blurItemStyle = itemModel.getModel(['blur', 'itemStyle']).getItemStyle();
            const selectItemStyle = itemModel.getModel(['select', 'itemStyle']).getItemStyle();
```

and replace `RadarView.ts:244-245` with:
```ts
                symbolPath.ensureState('emphasis').style = zrUtil.clone(emphasisItemStyle);
                symbolPath.ensureState('blur').style = zrUtil.clone(blurItemStyle);
                symbolPath.ensureState('select').style = zrUtil.clone(selectItemStyle);
```

This mirrors the canonical symbol path in `src/chart/helper/Symbol.ts:248-250` and `:335-339`:
